Z||000023||banditbalz||11-08-2001||09:56 PM||||fropuff, Lothar's turbo 2.8 came in at 15.3 to Tim's NOS 15.4<BR>I raced the NOS and we were side by side down the strip. I edged him out by two tenths of a second, so the race was close!  Tim has a 70 shot (10lb bottle) with a bottle warmer. He uses a remote bottle opener. Not sure if he purges or not. <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||grinthock||11-08-2001||10:02 PM||||Bandit:    Tim's not purging, he was talking about doing it.    He doesn't open till the last minute.  <P><BR>Slammed.  I gotta agree, I drove that black turbo car before he got it, didn't seem THAT fast.  It lags pretty bad.  As for Tim's NOS powered car somethings up.  I have a 2.8 ported exhaust with a Crane CAM, I turn a 15.7 with mine NO PROBLEMS, havn't had mine out at the track enough, plus I had some ignition issues when I was there doing 15.7's.<P>He should be into 14's with that 3.1<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
